# VTID-03801 — commands actually run.

# --- Investigation --------------------------------------------------------
# User reported (two screenshots): Chinese Notification Settings and
# Turkish My Journey both showing German content despite the language
# switch. Dispatched a research agent for file:line evidence, then
# personally re-verified every claim by reading the actual source before
# writing any fix.

grep -n "resolveLocale" services/gateway/src/routes/journey-checklist.ts
#   -> confirmed the established `?locale=` override pattern already used
#      by My Journey's own route.

grep -n "'de' | 'en' | 'es' | 'sr'" services/gateway/src/i18n/catalog.ts
#   -> confirmed GatewayLocale had no 'tr' member at all.

# Direct DB check (read-only) confirmed journey_checklist_translations
# already had 252/254 tr rows — i.e. this was a registration bug, not a
# missing-content bug, unlike ar (VTID-03644) which shipped genuinely
# empty.

grep -n "GatewayLocale" services/gateway/src/routes/user-category-preferences.ts
#   -> confirmed the route had no ?locale= handling of any kind, unlike
#      journey-checklist.ts.

# --- Fix -------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Registered 'tr' as a first-class GatewayLocale.
#    - src/i18n/catalog.ts: added 'tr' to the GatewayLocale union and
#      GATEWAY_LOCALES array, imported/registered tr.json, added
#      LANGUAGE_NAME_TO_LOCALE / LOCALE_ENGLISH_NAME / LOCALE_INFORMAL_HINT
#      entries.
#    - src/i18n/locales/tr.json (new): full 114/114-key Turkish
#      translation, informal sen-form register, verified against de.json
#      key-for-key via a diff script (zero missing, zero extra keys).

# 2. Added the ?locale= override to the category-preferences route,
#    mirroring journey-checklist.ts's resolveLocale():
#    - src/routes/user-category-preferences.ts: new exported
#      resolveRequestedLocale(), used ahead of getUserLocale().

# 3. Fixed the two resulting tsc failures — exhaustive
#    Record<GatewayLocale,...> maps that fail the build when a new locale
#    is added without a corresponding entry:
cd services/gateway
npx tsc --noEmit
#   -> 2 errors: llm-locale.ts (LANGUAGE_NAMES / REGISTER_HINTS),
#      feedback-settings-tools.ts (SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES). Added 'tr'
#      entries to both.
npx tsc --noEmit
#   -> clean. (outputs/tsc.txt)

# 4. Updated 3 pre-existing tests that hardcoded the 10-locale set:
#    - test/i18n/catalog-coverage.test.ts
#    - test/journey-checklist-translations.test.ts
#    - test/orb/live/characterization/tool-catalog.characterization.test.ts
#      (snapshot regenerated via `npx jest -u` — the set_language tool's
#      enum legitimately changed)
npx jest -u test/orb/live/characterization/tool-catalog.characterization.test.ts

# 5. New test for the route-level fix (resolveRequestedLocale exported
#    specifically for this):
#    test/routes/user-category-preferences.locale.test.ts

# --- Verification ------------------------------------------------------------
npx jest test/i18n/catalog-coverage.test.ts \
         test/journey-checklist-translations.test.ts \
         test/orb/live/characterization/tool-catalog.characterization.test.ts \
         test/routes/user-category-preferences.locale.test.ts
#   -> 4 suites, 68 tests passing. (outputs/targeted-tests.txt)

npx jest
